My guess at the situation: the individual had Magicbane alone for a
while and enchanted it to +7 when it was his sole weapon, either
favoring damage over magical effects or being unaware of the trade-
off.  Later, he decided to start two-weaponing, either when skill
slots became available or when he found the silver saber.  Since the
time he began two-weaponing, he's only had one enchant weapon scroll.

My guess to your question: the +7 Magicbane has a +5 to-hit advantage
over +2 Magicbane.  Usually by this time luck is high enough that
you're hitting pretty much anything anyway, but in theory the +2 will
miss more often than the +7, and when it misses the saber misses
also.  Thus the +7 over the long haul will be dealing more damage
because it has fewer attacks for zero damage.

